# The override log. Copy to `web/.env.local` and fill in the project's own values.
#
# Both are baked into the static build, and both are meant to be public.
# Ticket 03: the anon key identifies the project, not a person. Row level
# security is the whole protection, and the table has an insert policy and a
# select policy and NO update or delete policy — the absence of the policy is
# what makes it append-only.
#
# The `PUBLIC_` prefix is not decoration: Astro only exposes a variable to the
# browser when it carries it, and every read and write here happens in the
# browser. Without the prefix the value is undefined at runtime and the log
# reports itself as not connected.
#
# ANON_KEY takes either the legacy `anon` JWT or a new `sb_publishable_...`
# key. Never the service role key or an `sb_secret_...` key: those bypass row
# level security and this file ends up in a static build on a public webhost.
#
# Without these two the log still reads normally. Only the acting is disabled,
# and the page says so rather than dropping clicks silently.

PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
